# =============================================================================
# .gitignore for the Weighted Hydrographs / FPCA project
#
# PRINCIPLE: commit CODE and DOCUMENTS. Do not commit DATA or OUTPUT.
#
# Reasons: (1) GitHub rejects files over 100 MB and slows badly over ~50 MB;
# (2) anything committed lives in the history forever, even after deletion;
# (3) fish data may carry access restrictions.
#
# Everything ignored here is REGENERABLE by re-running the pipeline. That is the
# test for whether something belongs in the repository.
# =============================================================================

# --- R / RStudio -------------------------------------------------------------
.Rhistory
.Rapp.history
.RData
.Ruserdata
.Rproj.user/
*.Rproj.user
.Renviron

# --- data (regenerable or restricted) ----------------------------------------
data/
Data/
imputed_output/
*.rds
*.RDS
*.RData
*.csv
*.xlsx
*.xls

# --- model output ------------------------------------------------------------
output/models
Output/
JAGS_PVA/ModelFits/
JAGS_PVA/ModelOutput/

# --- figures (regenerable) ---------------------------------------------------
# Matches at any depth, so output/figures/ and manuscript/figures/ are both
# covered. manuscript/figures/ is a staging copy made by render_site.R; the
# published figures reach GitHub inside _site/ on the gh-pages branch, not from
# main, so nothing here needs an exception.
figures/

# --- rendered documents ------------------------------------------------------
# The site renders to _site/, which is ignored below and published to gh-pages.
*.html
*_files/
*_cache/
*.knit.md
*.utf8.md

# --- OS noise ----------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# =============================================================================
# EXCEPTIONS -- small files worth committing so the pipeline is reproducible.
# 'git add -f <file>' also works for a one-off.
# =============================================================================
!.gitignore
!*.Rproj
# NOTE: the standardization constants are saved INSIDE output/models/flow.rds and
# are regenerated by R/02_build_flow.R, so they are deliberately not committed.
# An earlier version kept an exception for data/flow_fd/*_climatology.rds; that
# path belonged to the previous pipeline and no longer exists.

# --- rendered website ---------------------------------------------------------
# publish_site.sh pushes _site/ to the gh-pages branch, so it does not need to be
# committed. If you would rather use the GitHub Actions workflow, DELETE the two
# lines below and commit the rendered folder instead.
_site/
.gh-pages-worktree/
manuscript/*_files/
manuscript/*_cache/
